Q: Use INNER JOIN or Sub-queries in a more efficient way A: <p>It seems to me that such a query is quite suitable for execution on the DBMS side.</p>
<p>And MySQL has all the tools for such operations.</p>
<pre><code>SELECT p.ProductID, p.ProductName
  ,json_object('ProductId',p.ProductID,'ProductName', p.ProductName
      ,'ProductMedia'
        ,(select json_arrayagg(json_object('ProductMediaPath',m.ProductMediaPath))
          from ProductMedia m where m.ProductID=p.ProductID
          group by ProductID)
      ,'ProductVariants'
          ,(select json_arrayagg(json_object('VariantID',v.VariantID,'VariantName',v.VariantName))
            from ProductVariants v where v.ProductID=p.ProductID
            group by ProductID)
      ,'ProductTags'
            ,(select json_arrayagg(json_object('TagID',t.TagID,'TagName',t.TagName))
              from ProductTags pt 
              inner join Tags t on t.TagID=pt.TagID
              where pt.ProductID=p.ProductID
              group by ProductID)
   ) obj
FROM Products p
WHERE ProductID = ?
</code></pre>
